cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Catastrophic Hydrotectonic Flood Model: A Layered Mechanism for Rapid Continental Reorganization"
message: "If you use this work, please cite the position paper below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Longmire
    given-names: James D.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1383-7698"
    email: jdlongmire@outlook.com
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-16"
url: "https://github.com/jdlongmire/catastrophic-hydrotectonic-flood-model"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jdlongmire/catastrophic-hydrotectonic-flood-model"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  A Lakatosian research programme reconstructing a historical, catastrophic
  hydrotectonic global Flood: a layered mechanism of impact-triggered continental
  hydroplaning for lateral translation and localized subduction-channel softening
  for vertical descent, within a Genesis-consistent chronology. Offered as a
  research programme with an explicit protective belt and a standing self-audit,
  not as a completed geophysical theory. Standing verdict at this release:
  unappraised, with zero discriminators yet evaluated against data.
# Top-level `type` is constrained by CFF 1.2 to software/dataset. This repository
# is a research corpus rather than software, so `dataset` is the closer of the two;
# the scholarly object to cite is the position paper given below.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "The Global Hydrotectonic Flood Model: A Layered Mechanism for Rapid Continental Reorganization"
  authors:
    - family-names: Longmire
      given-names: James D.
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1383-7698"
  year: 2026
  doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21972859"
  notes: >
    Position paper v0.1, published 2026-08-16. The published title reads "Global"
    because the programme was renamed to "Catastrophic" on 2026-08-18, after
    publication; the deposit's files are immutable. WP-HTF-0008 tracks the v0.2
    revision that reconciles the two. Concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21972858 always
    resolves to the newest version.
